      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is not just you; these phrases carry significant rhetorical weight. These linguistic anchors, often termed \"buzzwords\" or euphemisms, function to create a sense of inevitability and polished professionalism. They serve as narrative smoothers, signaling a transition where critical questioning is subtly discouraged in favor of accepting the status quo or the transition itself. This careful linguistic framing can indeed induce a psychological sense of cognitive distance, making the message feel less personal and more like necessary procedure.",
      "source": "target",
